{y:i}That will bring us back to

658
00:58:56,494 --> 00:58:59,956
{y:i}- Doe
{y:i}- A deer, a female deer

659
00:59:00,206 --> 00:59:03,460
{y:i}Ray, a drop of golden sun

660
00:59:03,710 --> 00:59:06,963
{y:i}Me, a name I call myself

661
00:59:07,213 --> 00:59:10,300
{y:i}Far, a long long way to run

662
00:59:10,550 --> 00:59:13,803
{y:i}Sew, a needle pulling thread

663
00:59:14,054 --> 00:59:17,474
{y:i}La, a note to follow sew

664
00:59:17,724 --> 00:59:20,310
{y:i}Tea, a drink with jam and bread

665
00:59:20,560 --> 00:59:24,773
{y:i}That will bring us back to doe

666
00:59:25,023 --> 00:59:28,318
{y:i}Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do, so-do

667
00:59:28,568 --> 00:59:33,156
Do-re-mi-fa-so and so on are only
the tools we use to build a song.

668
00:59:33,406 --> 00:59:36,618
Once you have them in your head
you can sing different tunes...

669
00:59:36,868 --> 00:59:39,996
...by mixing them up. Like this:

670
00:59:40,246 --> 00:59:45,752
{y:i}So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re

671
00:59:46,002 --> 00:59:47,045
Can you do that?

672
00:59:47,295 --> 00:59:52,759
{y:i}So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re

673
00:59:53,009 --> 00:59:58,682
{y:i}So-do-la-ti-do-re-do

674
00:59:58,932 --> 01:00:04,229
{y:i}So-do-la-ti-do-re-do

675
01:00:04,479 --> 01:00:06,189
Now, put it all together.

676
01:00:06,439 --> 01:00:13,071
{y:i}So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re

677
01:00:13,321 --> 01:00:19,577
{y:i}So-do-la-ti-do-re-do

678
01:00:19,828 --> 01:00:22,455
- Good.
- But it doesn't mean anything.

679
01:00:22,706 --> 01:00:25,667
So we put in words.
One word for every note.

680
01:00:25,917 --> 01:00:27,168
Like this:

681
01:00:27,419 --> 01:00:33,967
{y:i}When you know the notes to sing

682
01:00:34,217 --> 01:00:39,889
{y:i}You can sing most anything

683
01:00:40,140 --> 01:00:41,057
Together!

684
01:00:41,307 --> 01:00:48,023
{y:i}When you know the notes to sing

685
01:00:48,273 --> 01:00:55,113
{y:i}You can sing most anything

686
